  "content": {
    "summary": {
      "text": "The report concerns parameter-ID generation for a parametrized custom object whose `__getattr__` raises `KeyError` when pytest probes `__name__`. Maintainers treated explicit parameter IDs as the appropriate workaround, but the absence of a minimal reproducer and exact pytest version prevents verifying the claimed regression. The issue is closed as not planned.",
      "source_ids": [
        "S1",
        "S2",
        "S4",
        "S10"
      ]
    },
    "known_facts": [
      {
        "text": "The reporter received `KeyError: '__name__'` from `_idval_from_value` while using a custom dictionary-wrapper instance as a parametrized value; replacing it with a regular dictionary reportedly avoided the error.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The reporter later explained that the custom `DotDict` assigned `__getattr__` and `__setattr__` to item-access methods. They reported that changing the fallback behavior for undefined attributes avoided the failure.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S2",
          "S5",
          "S7"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A maintainer explained that an instance whose `__getattr__` raises `KeyError` is problematic for normal attribute probing and recommended supplying an explicit parameter ID, with the example `pytest.param(MyBroken(), id=\"broken\")`.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S8",
          "S10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The reporter said the same tests had worked about one week earlier, but the thread does not provide the exact pytest versions before and after the change or a minimal executable reproducer.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S4",
          "S12"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The current bug-report template asks for environment package output, pytest and operating-system versions, and a minimal example where possible; because it is a Markdown template, these items are not established as mandatory form fields.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S17"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "missing_information": [
      "What exact pytest version failed, and which exact version had previously passed?",
      "Can the behavior be demonstrated with a minimal test containing the `DotDict` implementation and one `@pytest.mark.parametrize` invocation?",
      "Were pytest or other environment packages upgraded between the last passing and first failing runs?"
    ],
    "draft_reply": "For later readers: this occurs while pytest is generating display IDs for parametrized values and probes the value’s `__name__`. In this report, the custom instance’s `__getattr__` delegated to item lookup and raised `KeyError` for a missing attribute; normal attribute lookup is expected to signal a missing attribute with `AttributeError`.\n\nAn explicit ID does not require modifying pytest internals. It can be supplied where the parameter is declared, for example:\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"value\", [pytest.param(DotDict(...), id=\"dotdict-case\")])\ndef test_something(value):\n    ...\n```\n\nAlternatively, the custom `__getattr__` implementation should translate missing keys into `AttributeError`. Because no minimal reproducer or exact before/after pytest versions were provided, the claimed regression could not be established from this thread.",
    "limitations": [
      "No source code or release history was inspected, and no reproduction was executed, so neither a pytest regression nor a current fix can be confirmed.",
      "Only the body of candidate issue #10184 was retrieved; its comments, linked changes, and historical resolution were not examined.",
      "The available issue-template lookup was partial and reflects the current default branch, which may differ from the template present when this issue was filed."
    ],
    "comparisons": [
      {
        "issue_number": 10184,
        "relationship": "possible_duplicate",
        "reason": "Both reports show parametrized-value ID generation failing when `_idval_from_value` probes `__name__` and the value’s `__getattr__` raises `KeyError`. This supports a tentative duplicate relationship, although the object types and missing keys differ and the target lacks a minimal reproducer.",
        "similarities": [
          "Both failures occur during pytest’s automatic ID generation for a parametrized object.",
          "Both traces involve `getattr(val, \"__name__\", None)` in `_idval_from_value`.",
          "In both cases, custom or delegated attribute access raises `KeyError` instead of returning a value or raising `AttributeError`."
        ],
        "differences": [
          "The target uses a custom dictionary wrapper and reports `KeyError: '__name__'`.",
          "Issue #10184 supplies a complete reproducer using `urllib.request.HTTPError`, whose delegated attribute access raises `KeyError: 'file'`.",
          "Issue #10184 identifies pytest 7.1.2 and Python 3.10.5, while the target only exposes a Python 3.14 installation path and does not identify the pytest version."
        ],
        "source_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S15"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "label_recommendations": [
      {
        "name": "topic: parametrize",
        "reason": "The failure occurs while pytest processes a value supplied to a parametrized test and generates its parameter ID.",
        "source_ids": [
          "S1",
          "S13"
        ]
      }
    ]
